  "answer": "A synapse is the functional region of contact between two neurons where information is transmitted from one neuron to another. It is a gap across which signals are passed either in the form of chemical or electrical signals. When a stimulus is received by the dendrites of a neuron, it sets off a chemical reaction that creates an electrical impulse. This impulse is transmitted through the cell body and axon. The chemicals from the axon cross the synapse and reach the next neuron, allowing the transfer of information across the nervous system.",
